the maintenance of discipline among the students of the Institute;
(i)
the fees to be charged for courses of study at the Institute and for admission to the examinations;
(j)
the conditions of residence of students of the Institute and the levying of the fees for residence in the halls and hostels
and of other charges; and
(k)
any other matter which by this Act or the Statutes is to be, or may be, provided for by the Ordinances.
